{"strongs": "H0374", "word": "אֵיפָה", "translit": "e.phah", "root": "איפה", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "ephah", "definition": "אֵיפָה 35 , אֵפָה noun feminine ephah (etymology dubious, ᵐ5 . οιφι etc., compare Coptic ôipi , Thes Lag Or. ii. 2 & cit .) — ׳ א Num 5:15 +; אֵפָה Exod 16:36 +; construct אֵיפַת Lev 19:36 +; — ephah , a grain-measure. 1. a certain quantity of wheat, barley, etc. = ten omers ( עֹמֶר ) Exod 16:36 (compare in measure of offerings Lev 5:11 ; Lev 6:13 ; Num 5:15 ; Num 28:5 , all ׳ עֲשִׂירִית הָא ; = 1/10 chomer ( חֹמֶר ) Ezek 45:11 (= bath, בַּת , liquid measure q. v.) compare Isa 5:10 chiefly of offerings, see above & 1Sam 1:24 ; Ezek 45:13 (twice in verse); Ezek 45:24 (3 t. in verse); Ezek 46:5 (twice in verse); Ezek 46:7 (3 t. in verse); Ezek 46:11 (3 t. in verse); Ezek 46:14 compare Judg 6:19 , but also of food 1Sam 17:17 compare Ruth 2:17 & Isa 5:10 above 2. receptacle or measure, holding an ephah, in prophetic vision Zech 5:6 ; Zech 5:7 ; Zech 5:8 ; Zech 5:9 ; Zech 5:10 just measure אֵיפַתצֶֿדֶק Lev 19:36 (|| ׳ מאֹזְנֵיצֿ , ׳ אַבְנֵיצֿ , ׳ הִֶין צ ) compare Ezek 45:10 ; Ezek 45:11 אֵיפָה ׳ שׁלֵמָה וָצ Deut 25:15 (|| ׳ וָצ ׳ אֶבֶן שׁ ); of unjust measure אֵיפָה וְאֵיפָה Deut 25:14 ; Prov 20:10 ׳ הַקְטִין א Amos 8:5 אֵיפַת רָווֺן Mic 6:10 . (On the actual size of ephah, compare בַּת ). אֵיפֹה see below אַי . P.33", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB387')\">BDB387</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H374')\">H374</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB386')\">BDB386</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB388')\">BDB388</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>אֵיפָה</bdbheb><sub>35</sub>, <bdbheb>אֵפָה</bdbheb> <b>noun feminine</b> <highlightword>ephah</highlightword> (etymology dubious, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>. <grk>οιφι</grk> etc., compare Coptic <highlight>ôipi</highlight>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Thes')\">Thes</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Lag')\">Lag<sup>Or. ii. 2 &amp; cit</sup></lookup>.) — <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>א</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Num 5:15\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(4,5,15)\">Num 5:15</ref> +; <bdbheb>אֵפָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 16:36\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"36\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"36\" onclick=\"bcv(2,16,36)\">Exod 16:36</ref> +; construct <bdbheb>אֵיפַת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 19:36\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"36\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"36\" onclick=\"bcv(3,19,36)\">Lev 19:36</ref> +; — <highlight>ephah</highlight>, a grain-measure. <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> a certain quantity of wheat, barley, etc. = ten omers (<bdbheb>עֹמֶר</bdbheb>) <ref ref=\"Exod 16:36\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"36\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"36\" onclick=\"bcv(2,16,36)\">Exod 16:36</ref> (compare in measure of offerings <ref ref=\"Lev 5:11\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(3,5,11)\">Lev 5:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 6:13\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(3,6,13)\">Lev 6:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Num 5:15\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(4,5,15)\">Num 5:15</ref>; <ref ref=\"Num 28:5\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(4,28,5)\">Num 28:5</ref>, all <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>עֲשִׂירִית הָא</bdbheb>; = 1/10 chomer (<bdbheb>חֹמֶר</bdbheb>) <ref ref=\"Ezek 45:11\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(26,45,11)\">Ezek 45:11</ref> (= bath, <bdbheb>בַּת</bdbheb>, liquid measure q. v.) compare <ref ref=\"Isa 5:10\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(23,5,10)\">Isa 5:10</ref> chiefly of offerings, see above &amp; <ref ref=\"1Sam 1:24\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(9,1,24)\">1Sam 1:24</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 45:13\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(26,45,13)\">Ezek 45:13</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Ezek 45:24\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(26,45,24)\">Ezek 45:24</ref> (3 t. in verse); <ref ref=\"Ezek 46:5\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(26,46,5)\">Ezek 46:5</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Ezek 46:7\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(26,46,7)\">Ezek 46:7</ref> (3 t. in verse); <ref ref=\"Ezek 46:11\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(26,46,11)\">Ezek 46:11</ref> (3 t. in verse); <ref ref=\"Ezek 46:14\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(26,46,14)\">Ezek 46:14</ref> compare <ref ref=\"Judg 6:19\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(7,6,19)\">Judg 6:19</ref>, but also of food <ref ref=\"1Sam 17:17\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(9,17,17)\">1Sam 17:17</ref> compare <ref ref=\"Ruth 2:17\" b=\"8\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(8,2,17)\">Ruth 2:17</ref> &amp; <ref ref=\"Isa 5:10\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(23,5,10)\">Isa 5:10</ref> above </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> receptacle or measure, holding an ephah, in prophetic vision <ref ref=\"Zech 5:6\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(38,5,6)\">Zech 5:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Zech 5:7\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(38,5,7)\">Zech 5:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Zech 5:8\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(38,5,8)\">Zech 5:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Zech 5:9\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(38,5,9)\">Zech 5:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"Zech 5:10\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(38,5,10)\">Zech 5:10</ref> just measure <bdbheb>אֵיפַתצֶֿדֶק</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 19:36\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"36\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"36\" onclick=\"bcv(3,19,36)\">Lev 19:36</ref> (|| <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>מאֹזְנֵיצֿ</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>אַבְנֵיצֿ</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>הִֶין צ</bdbheb>) compare <ref ref=\"Ezek 45:10\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(26,45,10)\">Ezek 45:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 45:11\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(26,45,11)\">Ezek 45:11</ref> <bdbheb>אֵיפָה</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>שׁלֵמָה וָצ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 25:15\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"25\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"25\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(5,25,15)\">Deut 25:15</ref> (|| <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>וָצ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>אֶבֶן שׁ</bdbheb>); of unjust measure <bdbheb>אֵיפָה וְאֵיפָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 25:14\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"25\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"25\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(5,25,14)\">Deut 25:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 20:10\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(20,20,10)\">Prov 20:10</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>הַקְטִין א</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Amos 8:5\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(30,8,5)\">Amos 8:5</ref> <bdbheb>אֵיפַת רָווֺן</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Mic 6:10\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(33,6,10)\">Mic 6:10</ref>. (On the actual size of ephah, compare <bdbheb>בַּת</bdbheb>). </p></div><hr><p><bdbheb>אֵיפֹה</bdbheb> see below <bdbheb>אַי</bdbheb>. P.33</p><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Num 5:15", "book": "NUM", "chapter": 5, "verse": 15}, {"raw": "Exod 16:36", "book": "EXO", "chapter": 16, "verse": 36}, {"raw": "Lev 19:36", "book": "LEV", "chapter": 19, "verse": 36}, {"raw": "Lev 5:11", "book": "LEV", "chapter": 5, "verse": 11}, {"raw": "Lev 6:13", "book": "LEV", "chapter": 6, "verse": 13}, {"raw": "Num 28:5", "book": "NUM", "c